    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "27 nuggets.\n\n27 cannot be formed from boxes of 5 and 8. The five consecutive totals 28–32 can all be formed, and adding boxes of 5 gives every larger total.",
      "worked": "For 27 nuggets, the possible numbers of boxes of 8 are 0, 1, 2 or 3. The remaining numbers of nuggets would be 27, 19, 11 or 3 respectively. None is a multiple of 5, so 27 cannot be purchased.\n\nThe next five totals can all be purchased:\n$$\\begin{align*}28&=4\\times5+1\\times8\\\\29&=1\\times5+3\\times8\\\\30&=6\\times5\\\\31&=3\\times5+2\\times8\\\\32&=4\\times8\\end{align*}$$\nAdding another box of 5 to these totals gives 33–37, then 38–42, and so on. Thus every whole-number total greater than 27 can be purchased.\n\nThe largest impossible total is 27 nuggets.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
